KNOWLEDGE The owner decided on 2026-10-21, in the chat {Fixer asks: How should I resolve the remaining health-check errors, which come fro — 2026-10-21 21:30:04}, to keep the former Agents Server sample Books in the hidden `agents/.legacy/` folder as inactive reference, unchanged except the opening `AGENT` keyword. The owner accepted that they keep producing lint warnings: no-effect commitments such as `META`, `INITIAL MESSAGE` and `USE`, and the shadowed Adam and Teacher copies. That is 83 warnings, the number the owner was shown. They include `RULE U` in `firemni-pravnik.book` and `social-media-manager.book`: Czech prose whose word "U" the keyword rule joins to `RULE`, so it is an unknown commitment. Hidden folders are excluded from Manager routing and goal discovery.
RULE Do not rewrite, convert, activate or delete the Books in `agents/.legacy/` to silence those accepted warnings, and do not ask the owner about them again; report them as accepted. Diagnose only errors or new kinds of problems there.
KNOWLEDGE Health-check tasks list only the first findings ("… N more"). Compare the complete `node bin/ptbk.js lint --json` output, or an earlier check's trace, not the truncated list. When `git log -1 -- agents/.legacy` still shows a2ccb80f45 and its warnings still number 83, they are the accepted ones.
KNOWLEDGE In this repository `node bin/ptbk.js` runs the in-development engine, which can be newer than the running service (0.119.0-30 while the service ran 0.119.0-29). Its lint then also warns that a configuration migration is pending. The engine leaves that warning out of health-check tasks, and an engine of the newer version applies and commits the migration itself, so do not edit `promptbookVersion` in `ptbk.json` for it.
KNOWLEDGE In the specification audit completed on 2026-10-26 (result commit e9c4ae787825888fd5cfb2665267af092a4334be), the owner's current `npm run check` ran only typechecking; `check:full` retained tests and package validation. Re-read `package.json` before retrying checks after owner changes, and report required-check success, focused regressions and unverified broader validation separately.
KNOWLEDGE `scripts/build.mjs` deletes shared `dist/` before rebuilding. Concurrent builds invalidated specification-audit test and packaging runs with missing modules; avoid overlapping builds with validation using that output, and do not treat a mixed-build run as reliable validation of the source.
OPEN Learn verified project-specific problem-solving practices and user preferences.
